    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d496">

                <pb facs="1564" n="1406" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1406"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Turkish Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial Legation of Turkey</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-06-04"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4,
                        1906</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: Some ecclesiastical
                    authorities transgressing their powers have been issuing letters of
                    attorney.</p>
                <p>As those instruments can be drawn up and authenticated in the Ottoman Empire by
                    the courts of the “shéri” and notaries only, I beg that your excellency will
                    kindly address to the proper quarter the necessary communications in order that
                    all instruments of that character unlawfully issued shall not be accepted by the
                    American authorities if ever presented to them.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, Mr. Secretary of State, the assurance of my very high
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chekib.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
